.TH STICKLER 1 "2026-11-27" "stickler 0.1.0" "Spectacle Line Manual"
.SH NAME
stickler \- deterministic Python unified-diff checker and recorded multi-model verdict reader
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstickler\fR \fICOMMAND\fR \fIFILE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBstickler\fR inspects unified Python diffs against six built-in naming, structure, and smell shapes at zero token cost, flags three ambiguous borderline patterns for recorded two-model arbitration, and prints twenty-one deterministic analytical reports over local diff and JSON files without network access.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBcheck <file.diff>\fR
Check a unified Python diff against the six built-in shapes (exits 0 when accepted, 1 when sent back).
.TP
\fBrender <review.json>\fR
Render a version 1 recorded review JSON document.
.TP
\fBreview <change_set.json>\fR
Review a multi-file change set including borderline flags and recorded model verdicts.
.TP
\fBsplit <split.json>\fR
Compare two named model routes side by side across one change set.
.TP
\fBrejudged <rejudged.json>\fR
Compare verdicts across two rejudging waves of the same change set.
.TP
\fBcensus <collection.json>\fR
Summarize set, file, objection, and borderline flag counts across a collection.
.TP
\fBcontested | pattern | files | borderline | outcomes <collection.json>\fR
Print collection-wide readings focused on contested flags, borderline patterns, files, or outcomes.
.TP
\fBverdicts | shapes | choices | categories | grounds | judgements | standings | states | flags | models <collection.json>\fR
Print collection-wide tallies and slices across verdicts, six shapes, model choices, categories, grounds, judgements, standings, states, flags, and models.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
Clean diff on check, accepted review on render, clean change set on review, or valid reading on the other eighteen commands.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Findings stand (sent back on check or render, or static/upheld stickler findings on review), or container depth overflow (> 9997) on render.
.TP
\fB2\fR
Unreadable, non-UTF-8, invalid-JSON, or schema-malformed input file (printing structured defects on stdout), or invalid CLI arguments (printing usage on stderr).
.TP
\fB120\fR
Closed output pipe on stdout or stderr.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check a unified diff in CI
.nf
.RS 4
stickler check examples/smelly.diff
.RE
.fi
.PP
Render a multi-file change-set review
.nf
.RS 4
stickler review examples/change_set.json
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compare two model routes on borderline lines
.nf
.RS 4
stickler split examples/split.json
.RE
.fi
